#X text 82 706 Right inlet not connected: mono in \, stereo out. The clap \; also goes dry to the output (right *~) \, as a mixer does \; with a send., f 64;
#X obj 60 770 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 794 0: signal left (mono)   \,  messages \; 1: signal right. Not connected: mono (the left input feeds \;   both sides of the reverb \, the output stays stereo) \; 2: messages (the same as inlet 0), f 64;
#X obj 60 872 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 896 0: signal left   \,  1: signal right \; 2: events: value <control> <0-127> <v>   \,  dump sverb ... \;   display <title> <value> on every change (lkdisplay \, OLED), f 64;
#X obj 60 958 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 982 <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. decay 80 \; val <control> <value>: in its unit \, e.g. val room 120 \; ctl <index> <0-127>   \,  params v0 .. v9: set by index \; defaults   \,  reset: all controls to the defaults of the mode \; send   \,  insert: dry 0 wet 1  /  dry 1 wet 0.5 \; get <control>: answers value <control> <0-127> <v> \; dump: answers dump sverb v0 .. v9 \, which restores them \; preset ambient   \,  clear   \,  mono auto|0|1   \,  print, f 64;
#X obj 60 1124 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1148 dry (0): level of the input in the output \, 0 ... 1 ... 4 (64 = 1). 0 for a send effect \, the mixer adds the dry signal. \; wet (63.5 = 1): level of the reverb \, 0 ... 1 ... 4. \; room (49.9 = 80 ms): room size 10 ... 100 ... 200 ms (1 ms is about 1 foot). Sets the spread of all delay lengths \, changes are cross-faded. \; decay (41.2 = 1 s): RT20 \, the time to fall by 20 dB \, 0.01 ... 2 ... 30 s. To -60 dB it takes three times as long. \; early (87.9 = 1.5): level of the early reflections \, 0 ... 1 ... 2.5. \; detune (34.6 = 2): slow pitch movement inside the feedback loop \, 0 ... 5 ... 50. Breaks up metallic ringing \, high values make a chorus tail. \; lowcut (63.5 = 80 Hz): high-pass at the output \, 10 ... 80 ... 500 Hz. \; lowdamp (40.6 = 1.5): see Damping. \; highcut (106.4 = 12 kHz): low-pass at the output \, 1 ... 5 ... 20 kHz. \; highdamp (78.2 = 2.5): see Damping., f 64;
#X obj 60 1466 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Damping 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1494 The tail loses lows and highs faster than the middle \, as in a real room. The shelf filters sit inside the feedback loop: lows below lowcut + 100 Hz \, highs above highcut / 2., f 64;
#X obj 460 1570 s \$0-sverb;
#X floatatom 60 1546 6 0 127 0 - \$0-n-lowdamp -;
#X msg 60 1570 lowdamp \$1;
#X floatatom 160 1546 6 0 127 0 - \$0-n-highdamp -;
#X msg 160 1570 highdamp \$1;
#X text 82 1600 lowdamp (1.5): how much faster the lows decay than decay says \, 1 ... 2 ... 10 (1 = not faster). \; highdamp (2.5): the same for the highs. Higher values give a darker tail., f 64;
#X obj 60 1678 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Values\ in\ units\ and\ modes 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 1706 s \$0-sverb;
#X msg 60 1706 val room 150;
#X msg 190 1706 val decay 8;
#X msg 320 1706 val highcut 6000;
#X msg 60 1740 val lowcut 200;
#X msg 190 1740 preset ambient;
#X msg 320 1740 clear;
#X msg 60 1774 send;
#X msg 190 1774 insert;
#X msg 320 1774 mono 1;
#X msg 60 1808 mono 0;
#X msg 190 1808 mono auto;
#X msg 320 1808 get decay;
#X text 82 1842 val <control> <value>: sets a control in its own unit (ms \, s \, Hz \, gain) \, the same curve as 0-127 the other way round. \; preset ambient: the preset of Signalsmith Basics (long \, dark \, detuned) \, dry stays. \; clear: empties the reverb \, the tail stops at once. \; send \, insert: dry 0 wet 1 (the default) or dry 1 wet 0.5 \, the other controls stay. [sverb~ insert] starts as insert. \; mono 1 \, 0 \, auto: mono input on \, off \, or from the connection (default): with nothing connected to the right inlet the left input goes into both sides of the reverb. The output is stereo either way., f 64;
#X obj 60 2264 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ the\ reverb\ works 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2288 An FDN (feedback delay network) of 8 channels. The stereo input is spread onto the 8 channels and goes through two diffusion steps: each a set of 8 delays of different length followed by a Hadamard matrix \, which mixes every channel into every other. One click becomes 64 echoes. \; The feedback loop: 8 delays with lengths spread over about 0.7 to 1.4 x room \, a Householder matrix mixes them \, then the low and high shelves (damping) and the decay gain \, set from decay and room so the level falls 20 dB in decay seconds. Three of the 8 delays are modulated by a slow LFO (detune). \; Early reflections: a separate set of delays taps the diffused input once \, without feedback \, and adds it to the tail (early). \; Two more diffusion steps after the loop \, then the 8 channels are folded back to stereo and filtered (lowcut \, highcut). Left and right come from different mixes of the 8 channels \, so even a mono input gives a wide \, decorrelated stereo tail. \; All delay lengths derive from room with fixed random seeds \, a change of room fades between the old and the new lengths. In bela-workstation the LFO runs as a rotating phasor (cheaper on the Cortex-A53) \, the sound is the same., f 64;
#X obj 60 2032 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 2060 hradio 19 1 0 16 empty empty empty 0 -8 0 10 #fcfcfc #000000 #000000 0;
#X obj 220 2090 r \$0-sverb-out;
#X obj 60 2116 skpreset sverb-slots;
#X obj 300 2116 text define -k sverb-slots;
#X obj 60 2142 s \$0-sverb;
#X text 82 2170 Choose slot 0-15: the current slot is stored \, the new one loaded. An empty slot takes the current sound. The values are kept in [text define -k sverb-slots] and saved with this patch. The same logic as in skandrums and vrs23~: outlet 2 -> skpreset left \, skpreset left -> sverb~ (here through the bus)., f 64;
#X obj 60 2622 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Credits 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
